{"lines":[{"w":0.058270676930745419,"c":1,"y":0.074050225513073054,"x":0.17481202985833838,"h":0.016097875080489432,"t":"Test 2"},{"w":0.28979537963867186,"y":0.12015529913158529,"t":"READING PASSAGE 3","x":0.17463874234818652,"h":0.020603144928784234,"c":1},{"t":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 27-40, which are based on Reading","h":0.021417783600855667,"y":0.15948989098012423,"c":1,"x":0.17473829125201804,"w":0.77081085205078126},{"c":1,"x":0.1725777290441475,"y":0.17617855418514383,"w":0.15848486582438151,"t":"Passage 3 below.","h":0.019677269635320238},{"t":"MAKING THE MOST OF TRENDS","x":0.35150375849362625,"y":0.21656976744971457,"w":0.42293233235677086,"h":0.018895348808647183,"c":1},{"w":0.62996999104817708,"y":0.25334754080790267,"x":0.24984899181648093,"c":1,"t":"Experts from Harvard Business School give advice to managers","h":0.023059670570506174},{"t":"Most managers can identify the major trends of the day. But in the course of conducting research","h":0.020602543739372869,"c":1,"x":0.17286749597698331,"y":0.29211427883485874,"w":0.77079966227213559},{"y":0.31073750011343382,"x":0.17098880134131425,"w":0.70688690185546865,"h":0.019861032175234827,"c":1,"t":"in a number of industries and working directly with companies, we have discovered that"},{"y":0.32994186033397566,"c":1,"w":0.76879699707031257,"h":0.017450284128870841,"x":0.17105262919744244,"t":"managers often fail to recognize the less obvious but profound ways these trends are influencing"},{"w":0.75771794637044265,"h":0.021435791035275709,"t":"consumers' aspirations, attitudes, and behaviors. This is especially true of trends that managers","y":0.34542232891132429,"c":1,"x":0.17095275110586131},{"h":0.017489592950726385,"c":1,"t":"view as peripheral to their core markets.","y":0.36477784902373322,"x":0.1710526377699253,"w":0.32330825805664065},{"t":"Many ignore trends in their innovation strategies or adopt a wait-and-see approach and let","x":0.17098303042931387,"y":0.39519171977819534,"h":0.019381411982902996,"c":1,"w":0.71817082722981784},{"x":0.1709527233416813,"c":1,"y":0.41249072913364115,"h":0.021158757550595042,"w":0.75205576578776034,"t":"competitors take the lead. At a minimum, such responses mean missed profit opportunities. At"},{"t":"the extreme, they can jeopardize a company by ceding to rivals the opportunity to transform the","y":0.43303283990463859,"x":0.16917293543726486,"w":0.76503758748372397,"h":0.017707662588538398,"c":1},{"y":0.44909109162778416,"x":0.16907826312669519,"h":0.020392919001238408,"c":1,"t":"industry. The purpose of this article is twofold: to spur managers to think more expansively about","w":0.77837549845377607},{"x":0.16911000838725518,"h":0.018877180483904743,"t":"how trends could engender new value propositions in their core markets, and to provide some","w":0.74823476155598956,"y":0.46799610210039622,"c":1},{"w":0.74060150146484394,"c":1,"h":0.017707662588538287,"t":"high-level advice on how to make market research and product development personnel more","x":0.16917293334344957,"y":0.48679974218804956},{"t":"adept at analyzing and exploiting trends.","w":0.3272951253255208,"h":0.018696846381664578,"x":0.16906708413697052,"y":0.50424739490574788,"c":1},{"w":0.76315790812174478,"c":1,"h":0.016141863845658189,"y":0.53633720902806803,"x":0.16917292549979929,"t":"One strategy, known as 'infuse and augment', is to design a product or service that retains most"},{"y":0.55110926337977051,"w":0.75212544759114586,"h":0.022587684685387188,"c":1,"t":"of the attributes and functions of existing products in the category but adds others that address","x":0.16905098395537133},{"x":0.16907603623271256,"t":"the needs and desires unleashed by a major trend. A case in point is the Poppy range of handbags,","h":0.020001492497234707,"c":1,"y":0.57093033052019015,"w":0.77840637207031249},{"w":0.75770614624023436,"h":0.020146914627654944,"t":"which the firm Coach created in response to the economic downturn of 2008. The Coach brand","c":1,"x":0.16908431845291111,"y":0.58808323875616619},{"x":0.16910975830022787,"t":"had been a symbol of opulence and luxury for nearly 70 years, and the most obvious reaction","y":0.60749495507150653,"w":0.74259531656901046,"c":1,"h":0.021032086511772796},{"y":0.62645348824128066,"h":0.017461515133103012,"c":1,"t":"to the downturn would have been to lower prices. However, that would have risked cheapening","w":0.76127817789713559,"x":0.16729324178476104},{"x":0.1691729288606649,"c":1,"y":0.64230521584664158,"w":0.71616541544596357,"t":"the brand's image. Instead, they initiated a consumer-research project which revealed that","h":0.019031993205211095},{"w":0.77067667643229165,"h":0.018995492594977459,"y":0.66130070847018096,"x":0.16917294594738791,"t":"customers were eager to lift themselves and the country out of tough times. Using these insights,","c":1},{"c":1,"h":0.018995492594977459,"y":0.67868641330005075,"t":"Coach launched the lower-priced Poppy handbags, which were in vibrant colors, and looked","x":0.16917292562626055,"w":0.73496241251627603},{"w":0.74823460896809912,"c":1,"y":0.69767985953920642,"h":0.019436910546985042,"t":"more youthful and playful than conventional Coach products. Creating the sub-brand allowed","x":0.1672382035875655},{"c":1,"h":0.018998606621029257,"t":"Coach to avert an across-the-board price cut. In contrast to the many companies that responded","x":0.16909650295660175,"w":0.75765823364257823,"y":0.71557851882830603},{"x":0.16722390773928397,"w":0.75200586954752602,"h":0.019930269053422989,"y":0.73331246337908873,"t":"to the recession by cutting prices, Coach saw the new consumer mindset as an opportunity for","c":1},{"c":1,"x":0.16729323479716754,"t":"innovation and renewal.","w":0.19548871358235678,"y":0.75144880906111367,"h":0.014539562650288773},{"c":1,"t":"A further example of this strategy was supermarket Tesco's response to consumers' growing","x":0.16729323704543322,"h":0.019053519961915288,"y":0.78197674396413575,"w":0.73496241251627603},{"h":0.020406860577545927,"y":0.80027914884004914,"c":1,"x":0.16722526929141765,"t":"concerns about the environment. With that in mind, Tesco, one of the world's top five retailers,","w":0.75578837076822925},{"x":0.16541354155944465,"w":0.72744359334309883,"y":0.81831395349965375,"h":0.018895348808647183,"c":1,"t":"introduced its Greener Living program, which demonstrates the company's commitment to"},{"y":0.83575581381030806,"c":1,"w":0.74812026977539081,"x":0.16729324637796888,"h":0.019041353091837521,"t":"protecting the environment by involving consumers in ways that produce tangible results. For"},{"h":0.020021126643350984,"x":0.16724608411512434,"t":"example, Tesco customers can accumulate points for such activities as reusing bags, recycling","w":0.75010904947916657,"y":0.85374683753422942,"c":1},{"w":0.76891494750976563,"t":"cans and printer cartridges, and buying home-insulation materials. Like points earned on regular","h":0.019977109016177663,"y":0.87157947496202848,"c":1,"x":0.16723766348187288},{"t":"purchases, these green points can be redeemed for cash. Tesco has not abandoned its traditional","x":0.16729324178451491,"y":0.8924418601915981,"w":0.76127817789713537,"h":0.016122209434730306,"c":1},{"c":1,"h":0.01747368200318089,"y":0.90985189951814749,"x":0.16729322973343075,"t":"retail offerings but augmented its business with these innovations, thereby infusing its value","w":0.73496241251627603},{"w":0.25563908894856768,"x":0.16729323740943036,"y":0.92877906948834055,"t":"proposition with a green streak.","c":1,"h":0.015988372635703185},{"h":0.013081395234588733,"t":"46","x":0.16729323270787788,"w":0.024436090787251785,"y":0.96075581395115184,"c":1}],"h":3106,"w":2400}